# Journaling repository

**Scope:** This rule applies to the **journaling** repo only. It is the canonical place for **architectural decisions** and **how to edit files** here. When adding features, update this file if behavior or layout changes.

Companion rules:
- [`journaling-interaction.mdc`](journaling-interaction.mdc) — ask-first interaction rules (confirmations over assumed defaults).
- [`journaling-slack-formatting.mdc`](journaling-slack-formatting.mdc) — Slack mrkdwn rules for posted messages.

## Layout

| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `entries/YYYY-MM-DD.md` | One file per calendar day; hybrid capture (freeform + structured sections). |
| `reports/report-<audience>-<from>-to-<to>.md` | Period report (Markdown). Generated in full sets of four (see audiences). |
| `reports/report-<audience>-<from>-to-<to>.slack.txt` | Slack-mrkdwn sibling — **created only at post time** as a delivery receipt. |
| `plans/plan-YYYY-MM-DD.md` | Daily planning brief (Markdown). |
| `plans/plan-YYYY-MM-DD.slack.txt` | Slack-mrkdwn sibling — **created only at post time** as a delivery receipt. |
| `context/slack-<channel>-<from>-to-<to>.txt` | Fetched Slack channel history snapshot. |
| `context/jira-<slug>-<date>.txt` | Pasted Jira ticket / epic / project links + notes. |
| `.cursor/skills/journal-capture-progress/` | Capture / append progress into daily entries. |
| `.cursor/skills/journal-gather-context/` | Umbrella router for context gathering (prompt-only, no script). |
| `.cursor/skills/journal-fetch-slack/` | Fetch Slack channel history → `context/`. |
| `.cursor/skills/journal-fetch-jira/` | Save Atlassian links + notes → `context/`. |
| `.cursor/skills/journal-daily-plan/` | Two-phase daily plan: catch-up → confirm → save. |
| `.cursor/skills/journal-generate-manager-report/` | Build all four audience reports from `entries/`. |
| `.cursor/skills/journal-render-slack/` | Convert a `.md` (plan or report) to its `.slack.txt` sibling. |
| `.cursor/skills/journal-post-slack/` | Post to Slack (`chat.postMessage`); renders `.slack.txt` at post time. |
| `.cursor/agents/journaling-specialist.md` | Subagent: which skill to use and in what order. |
| `.cursor/skills/_shared/script_utils.py` | Token / `.env` helpers (tokens, install config, named channels). |
| `.cursor/skills/_shared/journaling_repo.py` | Resolve repo root; auto-creates `entries/`, `reports/`, `plans/`, `context/`. |
| `.cursor/skills/_shared/path_guard.py` | Keep file reads/writes inside this repo; size limits on reads. |

## Entry schema (`entries/YYYY-MM-DD.md`)

- **Frontmatter** (YAML between `---` delimiters):
  - `date` (required): `YYYY-MM-DD`, must match the filename.
  - `tags` (optional): YAML list of strings, e.g. `[work, project-x]`.
  - `audience` (optional): e.g. `manager_update`.

- **Body sections** (use these `##` headings so the report generator can parse them):
  - `## Freeform` — narrative; multiple captures the same day append as `### Capture <ISO8601>` under Freeform.
  - `## Wins` — bullet list (`- `).
  - `## Blockers` — bullet list.
  - `## Next Steps` — bullet list.
  - `## Metrics` — `- name: value` bullet key/value.

## Report schema (`reports/report-<audience>-<from>-to-<to>.*`)

- Generated by `journal-generate-manager-report` / `generate_manager_report.py`.
- **Default writes all four `.md` audiences** so the set stays in sync.
- **`.slack.txt` is never produced by the report generator** — it's written by `journal-post-slack` at post time (see **Delivery receipts** below).

### Report audiences (`--report-audience`)

| Audience | Intent | Shape |
|----------|--------|--------|
| `manager` | Leadership / exec-friendly | Short outcome paragraph from **Wins** + **Priorities ahead**; optional **Needs visibility**. No raw Freeform. |
| `self` | Personal reflection | Full **Wins**, **Blockers**, **Next focus**, **Notes** (freeform), metrics, sources. |
| `team` | Colleagues / shared context | **Highlights**, **Heads-up / dependencies**, **Coming up**. |
| `qa` | QA / validation | **Deliverables & changes**, **Risks / blockers**, **Suggested verification**, optional metrics. |

## Plan schema (`plans/plan-YYYY-MM-DD.md`)

- Generated by `journal-daily-plan` / `generate_daily_plan.py`.
- Two-phase workflow (see [`journaling-interaction.mdc`](journaling-interaction.mdc)):
  1. Catch-up from entries + optional `--context-file` → stdout (no save).
  2. `--save` only after user confirms → writes `.md` under `plans/`.
- `.slack.txt` sibling is written only at post time.

## Context schema (`context/*.txt`)

- Produced by `journal-fetch-slack` (Slack channel dumps) and `journal-fetch-jira` (Atlassian URL + note snapshots).
- Named with a date range (Slack) or a date + slug (Jira) so files remain navigable over time.
- Plain text; intended to be embedded in plans via `--context-file` or referenced inline during capture.

## Date-range behavior (reports)

- **Inclusive** `--from` and `--to` (both ends included).
- Only days that have an existing `entries/YYYY-MM-DD.md` file appear in the report (missing days are skipped, not errors).

## Delivery receipts (Slack)

`.slack.txt` siblings under `reports/` and `plans/` have a specific meaning:

- **Present** ⇒ the accompanying `.md` was delivered to Slack by `journal-post-slack`.
- **Absent** ⇒ the `.md` has **never been posted**.

To find unposted content, list `.md` files without a `.slack.txt` sibling:

```bash
for md in reports/*.md plans/*.md; do
  [ -f "${md%.md}.slack.txt" ] || echo "unposted: $md"
done
```

## Editing conventions

- **Do not** delete or overwrite a full-day entry without explicit user intent; prefer **append** via `append_journal_entry.py` or the capture skill workflow.
- Keep frontmatter valid YAML; preserve user wording in Freeform.
- **Secrets and install config:** store in repo-root `.env` (see `.env.example`). Never commit `.env`.
  - **Token:** `JOURNALING_SLACK_BOT_TOKEN` or any `SLACK_*` name.
  - **Default channel:** `JOURNALING_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID`.
  - **Channel aliases:** any `JOURNALING_SLACK_CHANNEL_ID_<NAME>` (e.g. `_SELF`, `_TEAM`, `_DEV_QA`, `_BENJI3_DEV`). Reference on the CLI via `--channel-name <name>`.
  - **Optional user:** `JOURNALING_SLACK_USER_ID` — your member ID (`U…`); used with `post_slack_message.py --prepend-user-mention` and `generate_manager_report.py --report-audience self --format slack`.
  - **Jira base URL (optional):** `JOURNALING_JIRA_BASE_URL` — if set, `save_jira_context.py` enforces that all URLs are under this host.
  - Before posting: invite the bot to the channel; app needs `chat:write`.

## Security and privacy

- **Hardcoded secrets:** no API keys, tokens, or passwords in source, tests, or committed config — only env vars / `.env` (gitignored). Placeholders in `.env.example` are fine.
- **Sensitive data in logs:** scripts must not print request bodies, full Slack API responses, or token values. Status lines may name files or channel IDs only; avoid dumping user journal content to logs unless the user explicitly asked.
- **Sensitive data in errors:** on failure, exit with a short generic message — do not echo stack traces, raw HTTP bodies, or token substrings to stderr.
- **Path handling:** `--file` / `--freeform-file` / `--output` / `--context-file` / `--note-file` resolve **inside this repository** only (relative paths are anchored to the repo root).
- **SSRF:** Slack URL is fixed to `https://slack.com/api/chat.postMessage` / `conversations.history` (no user-controlled URLs). Jira is link-only (no API calls).
- **Slack posting:** `--channel` must be an ID (`C…` / `G…` / `D…`), not a `#name`. Message length is capped to Slack's `chat.postMessage` text limit. Message **body** must follow [`journaling-slack-formatting.mdc`](journaling-slack-formatting.mdc).

